00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:36.275
So this gets further compounded if we add necessary fields like color,

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:40.116
icon, image. Solution: an appearance lexicon for badges.

00:07:41.816 --> 00:07:43.817
Okay, so this is it.

00:07:44.417 --> 00:07:48.578
community.lexicon.badge.appearance defines the user-facing presentation

00:07:48.678 --> 00:07:49.398
for a badge.

00:07:50.038 --> 00:07:53.599
A badge definition represents the stable badge being awarded.

00:07:53.799 --> 00:07:56.239
It has a unique name and unchangeable description.

00:07:57.819 --> 00:08:00.260
Recipients can trust

00:08:06.161 --> 00:08:09.382
that the meaning of the badge they hold will not change under them.

00:08:10.282 --> 00:08:10.662
Okay, so

00:08:12.943 --> 00:08:13.403
this is

00:08:15.163 --> 00:08:15.923
the definition.

00:08:15.963 --> 00:08:17.804
There's two parts: the definition and appearance.

00:08:18.624 --> 00:08:21.084
Recipients can trust that the meaning of the badge they hold will not

00:08:21.144 --> 00:08:21.984
change under them.

00:08:22.305 --> 00:08:25.345
Badge appearance represent how that badge should be displayed, visual,

00:08:25.405 --> 00:08:26.805
scoping, and link to learn more.

00:08:27.326 --> 00:08:30.666
This separates two concerns that are currently conflated, stable

00:08:30.746 --> 00:08:34.647
identity and mutable presentation, what the badge is versus what the

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:38.728
badge looks like, allows for progressive enhancement and extensibility.

00:08:40.228 --> 00:08:44.190
While this badge conflation has been a recurring issue, this is actually

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:49.112
a recurring issue, I think, everywhere, and I should write about it

00:08:49.212 --> 00:08:51.553
because I would like people to think.

00:08:54.614 --> 00:08:56.554
